  "description": "Normative CIP-39 v2 gas vectors. Cycles and cells recompute from the constants block for every vector. Every branch of an instruction is charged exactly the reads, writes and cells its CIP-39 section 15.1 row reserves; a successful branch also performs them. A vector with \"rejected\": true is a rejection path: it is charged its full reservation, persists nothing, and its state_reads and state_writes are null because the document fixes no order over admission checks, so how far a rejection got before failing is an implementation's choice. Branch cycles differ by decoded_instruction_bytes, whether the variation comes from an Option or from a variable-length vector such as endpoints. Only TopUpAccount creates an account, and only CreateStream reads cbqs.stream_rate_per_block.",
